# XCU fuser
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The whole utility is XSI-shaded. Each test starts a sleeping child that
# holds a file as its standard input (or has the directory as its working
# directory) and asks fuser about it. The pids go to standard output and the
# rest to standard error; the combined form (both to one file) is checked as
# a whole. A user may need privilege to run fuser; a process of the same
# user is expected to be visible.

assertion  XCU.fuser.001
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       For a file that a sleeping child of the test holds open, fuser (and
           fuser -f) write the child's process ID to standard output, in the
           form blank and decimal number for each process, and exit with
           status zero.
test       t/001-pid-on-stdout.sh

assertion  XCU.fuser.002
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       Standard error begins with the pathname operand as given (or its
           resolved pathname) followed by a colon, and ends with a newline.
test       t/002-pathname-on-stderr.sh

assertion  XCU.fuser.003
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       With standard output and standard error going to one file, the
           result for one file operand is one line: the pathname and a colon,
           then for each process a blank, its process ID and zero or more
           alphabetic use characters.
test       t/003-combined-line.sh

assertion  XCU.fuser.004
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       With -u each process entry has the user name (or the decimal real
           user ID when there is no name) in parentheses right after the use
           characters.
test       t/004-user-names.sh

assertion  XCU.fuser.005
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       A directory that is the working directory of a process counts as
           used by it, and the use characters for that process include c.
test       t/005-current-directory.sh

assertion  XCU.fuser.006
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       For a file that no process uses, fuser writes no process ID to
           standard output.
test       t/006-unused-file.sh

assertion  XCU.fuser.007
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       fuser of a file that does not exist exits with a status above zero.
test       t/007-missing-file.sh

assertion  XCU.fuser.008
anchor     utilities/fuser.html#OPTIONS
class      untestable
when       XSI
says       -c lists the processes using any file on the file system mounted
           at a directory, and for a block special device holding a mounted
           file system -f restricts the report to the device file itself.
reason     Needs a mount point or a mounted block device under the test's
           control, which a script cannot create portably.
